<header><p class="st-kicker">prince bishopric · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Prince-Bishopric of Lebus</h1><p class="st-meta">1252 CE – 1598 CE (approx.) · capital Fürstenwalde</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Frontier bishopric on the Oder that passed from Polish to Brandenburg control and was absorbed by the Hohenzollern electors after the Reformation.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The bishopric of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebou-people">Lebus</a> was founded in the early 12th century by the Polish dukes, under the archdiocese of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gniezno">Gniezno</a>. When the margraves of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> seized the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/land-of-lebus">Land of Lebus</a> around 1249 to 1252, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> came under their influence while keeping estates on both banks of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oder-river">Oder</a>. They moved their seat to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/furstenwalde">Fürstenwalde</a> in the late 14th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The territory was small and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> weak, caught between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-silesia">Silesia</a>. They held lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/furstenwalde">Fürstenwalde</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebou-people">Lebus</a> and Storkow and depended on the Brandenburg <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a>, who effectively nominated them. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> the electors installed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hohenzollern">Hohenzollern</a> administrators, and the see became Lutheran.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the last administrator, the bishopric was dissolved and absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/margraviate-of-brandenburg">Margraviate of Brandenburg</a> in 1598. Its lands west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oder-river">Oder</a> remain in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>, those east of it in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="prince bishopric, 1252 CE – 1598 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M30 82 V46 Q50 12 70 46 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 30 V82 M40 58 H60"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">prince bishopric</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:84.62%;width:6.89%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1252 CE – 1598 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>prince bishopric</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Fürstenwalde</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism, then Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Polish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>, <a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hochstift Lebus</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1425&amp;focus=prince-bishopric-of-lebus" aria-label="Prince-Bishopric of Lebus on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4996 370 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Prince-Bishopric of Lebus lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5316 626L5282 625"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5282 625h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5316 626h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5316 626h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Fürstenwalde. <a href="/atlas?year=1425&amp;focus=prince-bishopric-of-lebus">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
